			"url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/issues/11014",
			"summary": "A maintainer opens a collection point for how the IDE should behave when typing breaks attribute or derive macro input, which makes macros emit only a compile error and kills completions. They list options (ask macro authors to recover, keep the original item when the expansion is just a compile error, repair the input syntax before expanding, or do nothing) and lean toward repairing the input, citing dtolnay's argument and asking IntelliJ Rust to align.",
			"actorId": 3757771,
			"actorType": "human"
		},
		{
			"id": "rust-analyzer-11014:comment:993649769",
